<http://data.silknow.org/event/a9e7dd5e-84c7-3871-92eb-fb3ad8d61e4c>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Worn by Miss Mary Hannah Chester (1820-1896) when she married Mr Woolmer on October 12th 1848. We also have the white patterned silk waistcoat worn by Mr Woolmer for the ceremony  (T.182-1927) and a blue silk dress worn by their daughter Mary Chester Woolmer in 1874 (T.181-1927). The donor related that the wedding dress was worn with a white silk coal-scuttle bonnet with a face frill inside the crown, trimmed with a spray of orange blossom and two veils (one draped over the front, one over the back.), and a shawl of cream-flowered damask with fringes. These have not survived."@en ;
        ecrm:P14_carried_out_by        <http://data.silknow.org/actor/6f0a716f-c9d3-3b44-86c6-e17ed74d6986> ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
        ecrm:P23_transferred_title_from
                "Given by Miss E. A. Woolmer" ;
        ecrm:P24_transferred_title_of  <http://data.silknow.org/object/50fe776d-b6b2-346a-808c-015bbe8ea94d> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Worn by Miss Mary Hannah Chester (1820-1896) when she married Mr Woolmer on October 12th 1848. We also have the white patterned silk waistcoat worn by Mr Woolmer for the ceremony  (T.182-1927) and a blue silk dress worn by their daughter Mary Chester Woolmer in 1874 (T.181-1927). The donor related that the wedding dress was worn with a white silk coal-scuttle bonnet with a face frill inside the crown, trimmed with a spray of orange blossom and two veils (one draped over the front, one over the back.), and a shawl of cream-flowered damask with fringes. These have not survived."@en .

